From c4acfc81083a4a7470db9eea9c6d0635ac6b3074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: n0madic <800462+n0madic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:34:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MPEG: route native IPU input to the active decoder

The menu preallocates two Sofdec players and starts the first. Capturing
the last-created player in the IPU sink sends its bitstream into the idle
second decoder, while GetPicture on the first waits forever.

Select the native input owner at GetPicture, retain FIFO backpressure
until then, and resume a pending transfer from its current registers.
CHCR polls must preserve STR for a native IPU transfer that is stalled.
Reset/recreation releases ownership and GetPicture reinstalls the sink
after deletion of a previous owner. AddBs/PSS pacing remains unchanged.

Test: two decoders are created and input starts before GetPicture; the idle second decoder must not receive it and the first player gets a 32x32 frame (fails before this change).
